### Unequal hero sizes and mid-distance gaps (2026-09-12)

Hero width controls are now 1.7, 4.6, 5.2, 2.4 and 3.4 km; height controls
are 1.5, 2.8, 4.1, 1.8 and 2.7 km, preserving the five azimuths and distances.
Two broad volume-texture samples modulate original mid-distance extinction.
The modulation blends in at 6-11 km and out at 23-34 km, preserving distant
cloud density. It reduces density between patches rather than adding more
small noise. This adds two texture reads per evaluated material sample; no
performance improvement is claimed for this distribution change.

Live captures distribution_144/000_review_opaque.png show the large/small hero
contrast and reduced mid-cloud coverage. Large hero underside shadows remain
an art concern. No new graph asset dependencies were introduced: the existing
owned CloudNoise input is reused. Shader compile/save: zero errors. Full profile
and syntax check passed, with unchanged distribution_inputs.json source hashes
across distribution_verification.txt. Baking map saved after temporary capture
cleanup; no new bake or preview validation.

